From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrii <andrii_chepurnyi@epam.com>
Date: Tue, 26 Aug 2025 17:19:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] HACK: do not enforce full ecam size

Since we are using only 16MB for the virt PCI ECAM region and do not
need the full size, as described in the specification for the real PCI
host device, the restriction on the 256MB size of ECAM can be removed.
Additionally, increasing it to 256MB will require modifying Android
u-boot to avoid overlapping of memory regions.

(cherry picked from commit 44874fd63ba407719ac9e2f93873ed9a5f685732)

Signed-off-by: Andrii <andrii_chepurnyi@epam.com>
Signed-off-by: Leonid Komarianskyi <leonid_komarianskyi@epam.com>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [downstream fork / BSP-layer delta; not submitted upstream]
Origin: https://github.com/xen-troops/qemu commit 44874fd63ba407719ac9e2f93873ed9a5f685732
---
 hw/xen/xen-pvh-common.c | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/xen/xen-pvh-common.c b/hw/xen/xen-pvh-common.c
index 51ff1fe8e..458bd9239 100644
--- a/hw/xen/xen-pvh-common.c
+++ b/hw/xen/xen-pvh-common.c
@@ -317,10 +317,6 @@ static void xen_pvh_init(MachineState *ms)
 
     /* Non-zero pci-ecam-size enables PCI.  */
     if (s->cfg.pci_ecam.size) {
-        if (s->cfg.pci_ecam.size != 256 * MiB) {
-            error_report("pci-ecam-size only supports values 0 or 0x10000000");
-            exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
-        }
         if (!s->cfg.pci_intx_irq_base) {
             error_report("PCI enabled but pci-intx-irq-base not set");
             exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
